<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>China: Cargo ship fire kills at least 25</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a99f20eb89c8a64ad27ede6a5e9aa9834dd6fb1c33fc5172f6e9a0ddfd9fc1e3</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T11:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-cargo-ship-fire-kills-at-least-25/a-79212704--ae3b308586a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-cargo-ship-fire-kills-at-least-25/a-79212704?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least five people are missing after a cargo ship caught fire at the port of Qingdao. The cause remains unclear.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc39b2cf321313444f7feb2bd82943d72c9b3e772a731683b7ec3fdf5e0c82fb</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T05:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China: English to be removed as a graded core subject?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d45551fcea889f351f268db9f370df376b5700779066aa537fcac36597e87435</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-english-to-be-removed-as-a-graded-core-subject/a-79199629--52f7a1cb9d3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-english-to-be-removed-as-a-graded-core-subject/a-79199629?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A university professor is calling for English to no longer be taught as a graded core subject in Chinese schools. Opponents argue that, in a globalized world, knowing English benefits the country and one's career.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the September 11, 2001 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:359678b7a879278cfecfc96046dcec23543ff3886a63d7ab50c9fd0b79689ae3</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918--22a07e00351f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 attacks were partly planned in Hamburg, via the so-called Hamburg cell, whose members played key roles in the plot. A look back at a day that shook up Germany’s approach to national security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran tightens social control with crackdown on cafes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1597d1ce37b3f2ac5650671dfde5e8e8983073eaa4be677bbc000e8dc3c2fc4b</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988--56f8af8e2572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities are keeping a close eye on cafes, fearing they could play a role in fostering anti-government sentiment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Ethiopia's constitutional reform gives PM more power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8fe16e17b8a5ada0ff4e617247bc3d1a9aaf028980db1af828d3727019da22bd</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-gives-pm-more-power/a-79172262--92eff7ca7862.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-gives-pm-more-power/a-79172262?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Does Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed stand to benefit from a planned constitutional reform in the country? A new presidential system would reshape political power — and could give him even more power in office.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Syria arms depot explosion kills at least 14</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5402983747137e5a257e32575c8060a2c6aeae6f6ae159cd7782992f2e79a403</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314--22d7b8669d08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion struck near the Syrian city of Sarmada in Idlib province in the northwest. The Defense Ministry said the weapons and remnants from the war were being stored temporarily at the site before being relocated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cambodia's floating schools hit by rising fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:292923f208538a6091dd13a4d21d9ebc23ba0d7089cc0b0886b2bc98d979412c</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008--dc2e9aeeea22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran war has sent fuel prices higher in Cambodia, squeezing families who rely on fishing and boats for their livelihoods. For children living on Tonle Sap, rising fuel costs pose yet another barrier to education.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: How  the 'house of sisters' threat split society</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56659e2e406b46a129225919221fdef238516c7cb332be89844076c8fb1e84c0</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163--b9de2b546f7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rumor has it that the 'house of sisters' is where kidnapped women from other Syrian sects are forced to convert to Islam. Nobody knows if it really exists, but it's being used to create communal tensions anyway.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63bbf3f442c98d4798bbfc631381f5583ad78932aa31b3e63004651db18f9651</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967--d423991a2cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cambodia's crackdown on scam operators is stranding young African trafficking victims in the Asian country with no money, no passport and no prospects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Putin rejects mobilization rumors, many Russians unconvinced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c0c754c2ba514f749d2275c52dda4ca25be102a3de9bb3d2ff0c6b9fe79a2a8</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386--b343555e2833.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia’s President Vladimir Putin has dismissed rumors about military mobilization. But many Russians, including many DW users, say they are preparing for the possibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
